 "scope_notes": "The production code change is only around 15 lines across src/flatfile.cpp and src/net_processing.cpp; the vast majority of the patch is test infrastructure and test cases simulating filesystem I/O failures.",
 "changed_since_previous": "The code and functional scope remain the same; only minor test adjustments or rebase updates distinguish this patch from the previous version.",
 "card": "PR 35003 ensures that block data I/O failures do not silently stall block processing or trigger abrupt assertions. If the block directory becomes inaccessible, FlatFileSeq::Open previously threw an exception that was swallowed by the P2P thread catch-all, leaving nodes running but stuck unable to connect new blocks. It changes FlatFileSeq::Open to return null on directory creation failure, changes GETBLOCKTXN read failures from an assertion abort to a graceful fatal error shutdown, and adds extensive functional and unit test coverage for disk access failures.",
